Chemostat is a Molecular Dynamics simulation method which maintains the bulk electrolyte concentration, implemented in LAMMPS (LAMMPS 11 Aug 2017 Version) (https://www.lammps.org/).

1. System requirements
System requirements of Chemostat are the same as LAMMPS software.
This package is supported for Linux, macOS, and Windows.
Please refer LAMMPS documentation for more system requirements (https://docs.lammps.org/Build_prerequisites.html).

Oracle Linux Server, 8.4 Version and icpc version 2021.3.0 (gcc version 8.4.1 compatibility) were used for compilation and simulation test.

Any non-standard hardware is not required.

2. Installation guide
git clone https://github.com/Minho-M-Kim/Cont.C
cd Chemostat/src
make mpi

Then, the simulation can be performed using lmp_mpi executable file.

5-15 minute is required to install on a normal computer

3. Demo
#Instructions to run on data
cd example_chemostat
Refer README file in example_chemostat directory

4. Instructions for use
a. Create a LAMMPS data or restart file based on the system of interests.
b. Write a LAMMPS input file based on the required simulation setup.
c. To use chemostat, fix conc/berendsen, group dynamics, .. are needed.
d. Run the simulation as in the demo.
